      "Factor the live step into (a) a *pure deterministic kernel* taking explicit (state, action, seed, opts) and returning a next state, and (b) a *thin orchestration wrapper* that threads defaults and calls the kernel. The wrapper preserves the live API; the kernel becomes callable by:\n      - The wrapper, in live operation.\n      - The predictive forward model, for candidate scoring — typically via a second arity that admits supplied candidate actions and skips the live action-selection step.\n    The predictive forward model then becomes a thin probabilistic wrapper around the same kernel: call kernel with candidate, add Gaussian noise (or other principled uncertainty representation), produce next-state distribution."},
